rol"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Both endpoints are near-isolated in this window (one event each): 1385\u2192639 and 1186\u21941818. Critically, 1186's only interaction occurs earlier in time than 1385's only interaction, so influence could not have flowed from 1385 to 1186 in any time-respecting order. The 600-unit reachability query fails and no paths exist; relaxing max_wait to 5000 or to unbounded still fails, ruling out the delay budget as the cause. A static connection does exist through the high-degree hub 639, and overall window activity is heavy \u2014 both classic confounders that are not supported by the temporal evidence."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion**\n\nEvidence chain:\n- 1385 has exactly one event in the window (\u2192639); 1186 has exactly one event (with 1818) [step_03, step_05, step_04].\n- Timing is fatal: 1186's sole interaction falls in bin [66349,71148], while 1385's sole interaction falls *later*, in [71149,75948] [step_14, step_15]. The target's only activity precedes the source's, so no time-respecting sequence can start at 1385 and end at 1186.\n- Direct check: temporal reachability with max_wait=600 reaches only 2 nodes and fails [step_01]; no paths enumerated [step_10].\n- Confounder controls: relaxing the delay to unlimited (340 nodes reached) or 5000 (112 nodes reached) still fails [step_02, step_13] \u2014 so the negative is not an artifact of the 600-unit gap budget. Ignoring time entirely, 1385 sits in a large 2-hop neighbourhood around the hub 639 (135 partners, 156 events) [step_12, step_09], i.e. a static/popularity-based connection exists but carries no valid temporal ordering. Overall window activity is substantial (5,532 events, 1,875 active nodes) [step_06], so volume alone would mislead. Intermediate 1818 is also unreachable from 1385 under the constraint [step_08].\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_20982933\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 639, 1818],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Both endpoints are near-isolated in this window (one event each): 1385\u2192639 and 1186\u21941818. Critically, 1186's only interaction occurs earlier in time than 1385's only interaction, so influence could not have flowed from 1385 to 1186 in any time-respecting order. The 600-unit reachability query fails and no paths exist; relaxing max_wait to 5000 or to unbounded still fails, ruling out the delay budget as the cause. A static connection does exist through the high-degree hub 639, and overall window activity is heavy \u2014 both classic confounders that are not supported by the temporal evidence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 55075, "total_output_tokens": 3959, "total_tokens": 59034, "total_latency_ms": 60932, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}